            <fr:title text="The Krull bound: only the upper bound is open">The Krull bound: only the upper bound is open</fr:title>
            <fr:taxon>proposition</fr:taxon>
            <fr:meta name="area">foundations</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="status">proven</fr:meta>
            <fr:meta name="provenance">journal sec:ideal.</fr:meta>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>Krull's height theorem gives <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\operatorname {ht} J \le  \frac {n(n+1)}{2}]]></fr:tex>
unconditionally, that is <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\dim  V(J) \ge  \frac {n(n - 1)}{2}]]></fr:tex>, and
<fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0007/" title="Flag witnesses for the partner variety" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0007/" display-uri="ffi-0007" type="local">the flag witnesses</fr:link> attain that lower bound.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Consequence.</html:strong> The whole content of <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0009/" title="The height conjecture" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0009/" display-uri="ffi-0009" type="local">the height conjecture</fr:link> is
therefore an <html:em>upper</html:em> bound on <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[\dim  V(J)]]></fr:tex>. The generators
of <fr:tex display="inline"><![CDATA[J]]></fr:tex> extend to a homogeneous system of parameters if and only if the conjectured height
holds.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:em>Uses:</html:em> <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0005/" title="The Steenrod ideal" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0005/" display-uri="ffi-0005" type="local">The Steenrod ideal</fr:link>, <fr:link href="/ffi/ffi-0007/" title="Flag witnesses for the partner variety" uri="https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0007/" display-uri="ffi-0007" type="local">Flag witnesses for the partner variety</fr:link>.</html:p>
          </fr:mainmatter>
        </fr:tree>
        <fr:tree show-metadata="true" expanded="false" toc="false" numbered="false">
          <fr:frontmatter>
            <fr:authors />
            <fr:uri>https://www.brendan.phd/ffi/ffi-0054/</fr:uri>
            <fr:display-uri>ffi-0054</fr:display-uri>
